  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    Orca raider of the Frozen Peace, raised by Grandfather Blood and trained by Krathund Gnurl. Rend Kzulrora bears a kelp-twist scar across his left flank — the work of Plunge-Caller Oeichowei, who deployed Hush☽ Twilight beyond Nightshelf jurisdiction. The wound never fully healed and still weeps salt. The maiming left him unable to dive to his former depths, a limitation he does not acknowledge and cannot conceal.
    
    He wears twelve penguin beaks on a fraying kelp-cord: not trophies but debts. Three were taken from his packmate Coldbringer Gnash Krukwark after Krukwark fell to the Augur's fire-hammer — *because someone had to keep counting*. He carries two artifacts from ☽'slew Nisaemesius~, the Nightshelf tunnel-colony: the Thrumed~ Shadow-glass and The Nighted~ Lantern, a forbidden tome claimed as the third of four successive thieves. He refuses to use either.
    
    Rend Kzulrora's principal role in the late Frozen Peace has been pedagogical. He teaches the Gut Inversion to younger orcas — a technique whose origins remain contested between penguin and orca traditions. Teaching, in his account, is what remains when raiding becomes a funeral march.
    
    When Grandfather Blood and the raider Ruibung faced an Aurora Stack tribunal for trespass at the sealed Drowned Ledge, Rend Kzulrora testified as cooperating witness and was released without sentence. He argued in hunt-speech that the Ledge had been abandoned, that Nightshelf records under Foedus∴silenti were fabricated, and that two maimed orcas near a ruin did not constitute a raid. He then told Luminary Xuzhong Pelm'Oath that he did not recognize penguin law — a statement that, whatever else it accomplished, cannot be accused of inconsistency.
    
    ☽'Otrolal the Watchful, the Nightshelf defender of ☽'slew Nisaemesius~, never killed him. The chronicles note, with what I take to be orca bitterness, that ☽'Otrolal never tried.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771589716268_0", anchor: "Nightshelf records under Foedus∴silenti were fabricated", text: "He was arguing in bad faith before a tribunal he openly rejected. But the Foedus∴silenti mandates collective silence regarding deep-cavern findings. A law that forbids truthful records does not fabricate — it ensures the only records that survive are ones someone manufactured despite the prohibition. Rend's accusation was cruder than the truth and closer to it than Luminary Xuzhong understood. What Rend could not have known is that his argument, stripped of bluster, described the mechanism exactly.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771589716268_1", anchor: "☽'Otrolal never tried", text: "In hunt-speech the words for *enemy* and *witness* share grammatical weight. To be hunted is to be seen. ☽'Otrolal saw other raiders. Not this one. In a theology where unwitnessed strength is nothing, that silence is the cruelest wound in the entry.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771589716268_2", anchor: "because someone had to keep counting", text: "The count belongs to the pod, not the counter. Krukwark fell; three beaks changed flippers like a ledger passed to a surviving partner. Whatever is being tallied here does not stop when individual mouths close.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
